ion/math-academy-id "q-2333" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}-{x}^{2}$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}-{x}^{2}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{7/2}-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =7{x}^{5/2}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=7(1)^{5/2}-2(1)=5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=5$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,1),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =5(x-1) \\\\ y & =5x-5+1 \\\\ y & =5x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-2333/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753/selection/feb54bcb082ae8c7fa1d7bb7ac7492a134afce3f3d9dbef4d910887225e02760" :answer/id #uuid "a13a08d9-fb2e-5f8d-b2e8-41dcc27977cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(28,-30)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753/selection/161f20358ea1a5aced164b71111ac6fa738af2442d9bc66871036d51e2388c37" :answer/id #uuid "ce2f2032-468b-5029-b572-e4405772ab5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-30)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753/selection/130916b6c8608d86eddbfa1dcadc2d22725f6e272a4a18f3bbaf46a7d5f7e50f" :answer/id #uuid "a339b011-a42a-59bf-860b-1c286e5c9790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(28,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753/selection/7e71fe8268d326e67e887834fa59bcc6916f20b4dacfd86231d5bb4352e18cf4" :answer/id #uuid "485bf178-da2c-5f97-8130-acb83206aa0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(30,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753/selection/36de6955e068baf8e57da4c7169388b90db1bb46c699933713dfc27ca30b4531" :answer/id #uuid "ae681b50-f2b7-531b-bd71-2e12d775f070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,28)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa1c4286-d0cc-5939-8b55-2b3276929aa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10753/selection/161f20358ea1a5aced164b71111ac6fa738af2442d9bc66871036d51e2388c37" :answer-field/choices ["q-10753/selection/feb54bcb082ae8c7fa1d7bb7ac7492a134afce3f3d9dbef4d910887225e02760" "q-10753/selection/161f20358ea1a5aced164b71111ac6fa738af2442d9bc66871036d51e2388c37" "q-10753/selection/130916b6c8608d86eddbfa1dcadc2d22725f6e272a4a18f3bbaf46a7d5f7e50f" "q-10753/selection/7e71fe8268d326e67e887834fa59bcc6916f20b4dacfd86231d5bb4352e18cf4" "q-10753/selection/36de6955e068baf8e57da4c7169388b90db1bb46c699933713dfc27ca30b4531"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10753" :question/id #uuid "98d3cf40-2059-5af6-a1da-8f71c594f15b" :question/math-academy-id "q-10753" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $f(x)=7{x}^{2}-2$ at the point $(2,26)$ intersects the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=7{x}^{2}-2.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{x}^{2}-2)=14x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2)=14(2)=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(26) & =28(x-2) \\\\ y & =28x-56+26 \\\\ y & =28x-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =28(0)-30 \\\\ y & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $(0,-30).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-10753/selection"]